# Deny everything, then allow back exactly what the image needs.
#
# Written as an allow-list rather than a list of exclusions on purpose.  A
# deny-list only protects against the junk you thought of; the source tree this
# stages from carries ~1.1M lines of uncommitted NPZ captures, 300k-line
# shot-run JSON, two 287 MB archives, W&B directories and __pycache__ across
# several Python versions. One forgotten pattern and any of it ships.
#
# With this inversion, a file enters the image only because it is named below.

*

# Build inputs
!Dockerfile
!entrypoint.sh
!train.py

# User commands
!bin/
!bin/mamba3-run
!bin/mamba3-ship

# Cameras 1-6 and their observers, staged by build.sh and deleted after.
!src/
!src/**

# Belt and braces: even inside the allowed paths above, none of this may pass.
# Nothing should match, and if something does, the build was staged wrong.
src/**/__pycache__/
src/**/*.pyc
src/**/*.npz
src/**/*.pt
src/**/*.safetensors
src/**/wandb/
src/**/results/
src/**/captures/
src/**/checkpoints/
src/**/.git/
src/**/.env
src/**/*.token
src/**/*.key
src/**/*.pem
src/**/.netrc
src/**/.huggingface/
